raph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/FileHandle.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FileHandle"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TName"},{"type":"text","value":">>"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const files = openaiFiles()\nconst handle = await uploadFile({ adapter: files, input: { data, mimeType: 'image/png' } })","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tname","text":"TName","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"adapter","text":"adapter","level":4},{"id":"input","text":"input","level":4},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction uploadFile<TName>(options): Promise<FileHandle<TName>>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/files/index.ts:27](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/files/index.ts#L27)\n\nUpload a file to a provider's Files API and return its handle. The handle\ncarries the provider name as a literal type, so passing it to another\nprovider's lifecycle call is a compile error.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TName\n\n`TName` *extends* `string`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### options\n\n#### adapter\n\n[`FilesAdapter`](../interfaces/FilesAdapter.md)\\<`TName`\\> & `object`\n\n#### input\n\n[`FileUploadInput`](../type-aliases/FileUploadInput.md)\n\n## Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<[`FileHandle`](../interfaces/FileHandle.md)\\<`TName`\\>\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst files = openaiFiles()\nconst handle = await uploadFile({ adapter: files, input: { data, mimeType: 'image/png' } })\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: uploadFile\ntitle: uploadFile\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction uploadFile<TName>(options): Promise<FileHandle<TName>>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/files/index.ts:27](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/files/index.ts#L27)\n\nUpload a file to a provider's Files API and return its handle. The handle\ncarries the provider name as a literal type, so passing it to another\nprovider's lifecycle call is a compile error.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TName\n\n`TName` *extends* `string`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### options\n\n#### adapter\n\n[`FilesAdapter`](../interfaces/FilesAdapter.md)\\<`TName`\\> & `object`\n\n#### input\n\n[`FileUploadInput`](../type-aliases/FileUploadInput.md)\n\n## Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<[`FileHandle`](../interfaces/FileHandle.md)\\<`TName`\\>\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst files = openaiFiles()\nconst handle = await uploadFile({ adapter: files, input: { data, mimeType: 'image/png' } })\n```\n"}
